<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">1 September in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 1 September, from 1057 to 1969.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/hagia-sophia" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hagia-sophia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1057">1057 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">969 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Isaac I Komnenos is crowned emperor in the Hagia Sophia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The general Isaac I Komnenos was crowned Byzantine emperor by the patriarch Michael I Cerularius in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hagia-sophia">Hagia Sophia</a>. He was the first reigning member of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/komnenian-dynasty">Komnenian dynasty</a> and ruled until 1059.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hagia-sophia">Hagia Sophia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1159">1159 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">867 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Adrian IV, the only English pope, dies at Anagni</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-adrian-iv">Nicholas Breakspear</a>, Pope Adrian IV, died after a stormy pontificate dominated by conflict with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa">Frederick Barbarossa</a>. His death led to a disputed election and an 18-year schism.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/papal-states">Papal States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa">Frederick Barbarossa</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1449">1449 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">577 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Oirat Mongols capture the Ming emperor at Tumu</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Under the influence of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eunuch">eunuch</a> Wang Zhen, the Ming emperor Zhengtong led his army against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oirats">Oirat</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> and was defeated and captured at Tumu fortress. The court enthroned his brother as the Jingtai Emperor and held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beijing">Beijing</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tumu-crisis">Tumu Crisis</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1715">1715 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">311 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Louis XIV dies after 72 years on the throne</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Sun King died at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/versailles">Versailles</a> days before his 77th birthday, having reigned for 72 years, the longest of any major European monarch. His five-year-old great-grandson succeeded as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xv">Louis XV</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/kingdom-of-france">Kingdom of France</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/versailles">Versailles</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xiv">Louis XIV</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1807">1807 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">219 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Aaron Burr is acquitted of treason</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A jury in Richmond acquitted former Vice President Aaron Burr of plotting to wage war in the West. Chief Justice <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-marshall">John Marshall</a>'s strict reading of treason doomed Jefferson's prosecution.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1864">1864 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">162 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Confederates evacuate Atlanta</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">General John Bell Hood abandoned Atlanta, blowing up ammunition trains as he left, and Sherman's troops entered the next day. The capture of the rail hub revived Lincoln's re-election hopes.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1923">1923 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">103 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Great Kantō earthquake devastates Tokyo and Yokohama</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A magnitude 7.9 earthquake and the fires that followed destroyed much of Tokyo and Yokohama, killing more than 100,000 people. In the chaos, vigilantes murdered thousands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/koreans">Koreans</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1939">1939 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">87 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Germany invades Poland</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">German forces crossed into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> at dawn without a declaration of war. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> declared war two days later, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a> had begun.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1969">1969 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">57 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Muammar Gaddafi seizes power in Libya</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Junior army officers led by 27-year-old <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muammar-gaddafi">Muammar Gaddafi</a> overthrew King Idris in a bloodless coup. Gaddafi ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/libya">Libya</a> for 42 years until his overthrow and death in 2011.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/libya">Libya</a></div></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 1 September <span class="n">5</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/gonzalo-fernandez-de-cordoba"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/gonzalo-fernandez-de-cordoba.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Gonzalo Fernández de Córdoba</span><span class="tp">1453–1515</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/william-iv-prince-of-orange"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/william-iv-prince-of-orange.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">William IV, Prince of Orange</span><span class="tp">1711–1751</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/jose-maria-castro-madriz"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/jose-maria-castro-madriz.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">José María Castro Madriz</span><span class="tp">1818–1892</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/joaquin-balaguer"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/joaquin-balaguer.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Joaquín Balaguer</span><span class="tp">1906–2002</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/abd-rabbuh-mansur-hadi"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/abd-rabbuh-mansur-hadi.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Abd Rabbuh Mansur Hadi</span><span class="tp">b. 1945</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 1 September <span class="n">3</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/foulques-de-villaret"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/foulques-de-villaret.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Foulques de Villaret</span><span class="tp">d. 1327</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/cornelis-de-houtman"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/cornelis-de-houtman.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Cornelis de Houtman</span><span class="tp">1565–1599</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/albert-speer"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/albert-speer.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Albert Speer</span><span class="tp">1905–1981</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
